# Tests of the `frames` module; generated from tools/frames.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

pushFrameTest is test
pushFrameTest purpose "Pushing a frame puts its name on top of the call stack; popping takes it off"
pushFrameTest verifies pushFrame keepsName
pushFrameTest verifies popFrame dropsTop
pushFrameTest typeParameter none
pushFrameTest input none
pushFrameTest output none
pushFrameTest outputOwnedBy none
pushFrameTest raises none
pushFrameTest effect use machine.memory
pushFrameTest effect use system.calls
pushFrameTest uses memoryAccess
pushFrameTest uses systemCalls
pushFrameTest memoryHeap false
pushFrameTest async false
pushFrameTest maxRecursion none
pushFrameTest label begin loopKind none
pushFrameTest label begin within none
pushFrameTest let name String "demo.main (demo.sem:9)" immutable
pushFrameTest let one Int64 1 immutable
pushFrameTest let zero Int64 0 immutable
pushFrameTest at begin do findState
pushFrameTest at begin do findCount
pushFrameTest at begin do readBefore
